<section class="py-section-gap bg-surface"><div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-margin-mobile md:px-margin-desktop"><div class="text-center mb-12"><h2 class="font-headline-md text-headline-md text-primary mb-4">Frequently Asked Questions</h2></div><div class="space-y-4"><details class="group bg-surface-container-lowest border border-surface-variant rounded-lg [&_summary::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden"><summary class="flex items-center justify-between p-6 cursor-pointer font-semibold text-primary">What is jaw bone surgery?<span class="material-symbols-outlined transition duration-300 group-open:-rotate-180">expand_more</span></summary><div class="px-6 pb-6 text-on-surface-variant text-sm">Jaw bone surgery, or osteotomy, involves cutting the jaw bones and repositioning them to correct alignment. The bones are secured in their new position using plates and screws, allowing them to heal in the corrected position.</div></details><details class="group bg-surface-container-lowest border border-surface-variant rounded-lg [&_summary::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden"><summary class="flex items-center justify-between p-6 cursor-pointer font-semibold text-primary">How long does bone healing take?<span class="material-symbols-outlined transition duration-300 group-open:-rotate-180">expand_more</span></summary><div class="px-6 pb-6 text-on-surface-variant text-sm">Initial bone healing takes 6-8 weeks, but complete remodeling can take 6-12 months. During this time, the bones solidify in their new position.</div></details><details class="group bg-surface-container-lowest border border-surface-variant rounded-lg [&_summary::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden"><summary class="flex items-center justify-between p-6 cursor-pointer font-semibold text-primary">Will I need my jaw wired shut?<span class="material-symbols-outlined transition duration-300 group-open:-rotate-180">expand_more</span></summary><div class="px-6 pb-6 text-on-surface-variant text-sm">Modern techniques often use titanium plates and screws that allow early mobility. Elastic bands may guide bite position, but complete wiring is rarely needed today.</div></details></div></div></section>
